How to run it

From the repo root:

# 1. build the client (repeat after changing specula-web)
cargo build -p specula-web --target wasm32-unknown-unknown --release
wasm-bindgen --target web --out-dir specula-web/pkg \
  target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/specula_web.wasm

# 2. start the server; it serves the page and the WebSocket on :8000
cargo run -p specula-server --release

# 3. in another terminal, join a game as observer
scripts/observe.sh HOST PORT

# 4. open http://127.0.0.1:8000

The server has to be started from the repo root, because it serves specula-web/ by relative path.
To open the page from another machine, start the server with ROCKET_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0.
Over plain http from a non-localhost address the browser won't offer WebGPU,
so the WebGL2 fallback draws. The browser console logs which graphics backend was picked.
